      en: { title: "Being", slug: "being", summary: "The most general concept of metaphysics: that which makes something be, as opposed to nothing.", definition: "\"Being\" names both the fact of existing and what all things have in common insofar as they exist. Aristotle noted that \"being is said in many ways\"; Heidegger reopened the question of its meaning.", etymology: "From Latin esse, infinitive of \"to be\"; corresponds to Greek eînai. The participle ón (\"entity\") gives rise to \"ontology\".", synonyms: ["Existence"], nearTerms: ["Entity", "Essence", "Nothingness"] },
      fr: { title: "Être", slug: "etre", summary: "Le concept le plus général de la métaphysique : ce qui fait qu'une chose est, par opposition au néant.", definition: "« Être » désigne à la fois le fait d'exister et ce que toutes les choses ont en commun en tant qu'elles existent." },
      de: { title: "Sein", slug: "sein", summary: "Der allgemeinste Begriff der Metaphysik: das, was etwas sein lässt, im Gegensatz zum Nichts.", definition: "„Sein“ bezeichnet sowohl die Tatsache des Existierens als auch das, was alle Dinge gemeinsam haben, insofern sie sind." },
