      en: { title: "Substance", slug: "substance", summary: "That which exists by itself and supports properties; for Spinoza, there is only one infinite substance.", definition: "Substance is what exists in itself and not in another, serving as the subject of properties or accidents. Aristotle identifies it with the concrete individual; Descartes distinguishes thinking and extended substance; Spinoza admits only one.", etymology: "From Latin substantia (\"what stands beneath\"), translating Greek ousía (\"essence\", \"being\") and hypokeímenon (\"substrate\").", synonyms: ["Ousia"], nearTerms: ["Essence", "Accident", "Substrate", "Mode"] },
      fr: { title: "Substance", slug: "substance", summary: "Ce qui existe par soi et sert de support aux propriétés ; pour Spinoza, il n'y a qu'une substance infinie.", definition: "La substance est ce qui existe en soi et non en autre chose, servant de sujet aux propriétés ou accidents." },
      de: { title: "Substanz", slug: "substanz", summary: "Das, was durch sich selbst existiert und Träger der Eigenschaften ist; für Spinoza gibt es nur eine unendliche Substanz.", definition: "Substanz ist das, was in sich selbst und nicht in einem anderen existiert und den Eigenschaften als Subjekt dient." },
