      en: { title: "Causality", slug: "causality", summary: "The relation by which one thing produces another; Hume reduced it to habit, Kant made it a category of the understanding.", definition: "Causality is the relation between cause and effect, by which one event produces or determines another. Aristotle distinguished four causes; Hume questioned its necessity; Kant established it as an a priori condition of experience.", etymology: "From Latin causa, of uncertain origin; Greek aitía originally meant \"responsibility\", \"charge\".", synonyms: ["Causal relation"], nearTerms: ["Cause", "Effect", "Determinism", "Necessity"] },
      fr: { title: "Causalité", slug: "causalite", summary: "La relation par laquelle une chose en produit une autre ; Hume la réduit à l'habitude, Kant en fait une catégorie de l'entendement.", definition: "La causalité est la relation entre cause et effet, par laquelle un événement en produit ou en détermine un autre." },
