      en: { title: "Induction", slug: "induction", summary: "Inference from the particular to the general; Hume showed it cannot be justified without circularity.", definition: "Induction is reasoning that generalises from observed cases to a universal conclusion or to future cases. The \"problem of induction\" (Hume) questions the rational legitimacy of this move.", etymology: "From Latin inductio (\"a leading in\"), translating Greek epagōgḗ as used by Aristotle.", synonyms: ["Inductive generalisation"], nearTerms: ["Deduction", "Inference", "Probability", "Causality"] },
